/* 
* This file is used when hosting on Cloudflare Workers. The actual static
* website is contained in docs/.
*/
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "website",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-05-25",
  "preview_urls": false,
  "assets": {
    "directory": "./docs",
    "not_found_handling": "404-page"
  }
}
/*
* 1. You MUST change "name: website" to *your* Cloudflare Workers project name.
* (Your URL will be {project}.{user).workers.dev).
*
* 2. You should keep the "compatibility_date" (yyyy-mm-dd) relatively current.
*
* 3. In mid-2025 (this may be fixed now), Cloudflare Workers created a preview
* URL even if you told it not to (in "workers > settings > build > builds for
* non-production branches."). It had to be set "false" here or a dev URL would
* be created.
*
* ADDITIONAL INFO:
*
* The following files are also specific to Cloudflare Workers, serving a similar
* configuration-like purpose:
*	/docs/.assetsignore
*	/docs/_headers
*
* The file "docs/.htaccess" contains more info about Cloudflare features I use:
*   1. "Bulk redirect" rule to redirect non-www to www.
*   2. "Security custom rule" to block prolific requests for things I don't
*		have (apparently looking for vulnerabilities).
*/
